title: 'For Drew: nothing in the drawing is shown wrong for Jeff''s example; build nothing for it.'
pid: 9b8ea017-0507-47eb-9b29-f7c285fbc635
body: |2-
  Jeff's example ([[id:c57a3db4-3962-4f1b-8bb0-4c557dad2ffe][example!]]) shows node 2fac9260 at its
  editable occurrence with M and nothing under it. That occurrence is in C, and its
  change leaf is a Text leaf (its title, a link, was retitled to another link), so
  'expected_change_viewnodes' in 'server/refresh/diff_view.rs' draws
  'ChangeViewnode::OldText' under it ('mk_old_text_viewnode' compares titles as
  text, so a link changed for another is a title change like any other). On a
  copy of Jeff's data as it stood when he opened the buffer, the server draws it
  there: '**** (skg (vnid 4m) (oldText title) ...)'. No node kind is missing; the
  old text has one. So of Top's three readings: there is no third way in the
  server, the property did have an old-value child, and the metadata was read
  right. If Jeff answers that the old title was not folded, the place to look is
  the client's redraw ('elisp/skg-redraw-delta.el', and
  'skg-replace-buffer-with-new-content' in 'elisp/skg-request-save.el'), which is
  Cleo's. Vic's two ways to meet a bare M at a write-protected occurrence
  ([[id:193c6781-d8b7-4036-9848-d740f0a2279f][Vic's note]]) are a separate matter, still awaiting Jeff.
